      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "KPZ supplied a remarkably simple universal mechanism for a broad class of far-from-equilibrium fluctuating interfaces, with unusually deep theoretical and experimental reach.",
        "attribution": "Kardar and Zhang established the defining theory; Takeuchi made exceptionally clean quantitative tests of its predicted universal fluctuations.",
        "maturity": "The universality class has been tested across many systems and its fluctuations are now understood with considerable precision.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Yi-Cheng Zhang's posthumous ineligibility complicates recognition of the original three-author formulation.",
