        "Alexander Polyakov",
        "John Cardy"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Conformal field theory transformed the understanding of criticality by identifying exact, universal structures in two-dimensional many-body systems.",
        "attribution": "Polyakov and Cardy are central architects of the physical framework and its applications to critical phenomena.",
        "maturity": "Its consequences are deeply established analytically, numerically, and experimentally, and permeate modern statistical and quantum field theory.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Alexander B. Zamolodchikov's posthumous ineligibility prevents recognition of all principal contributors.",
          "The proper boundary between this work and broader quantum-field-theory advances is debatable."
        ]
      }
    },
